{
	"$description": "The LAYOUT PRIMITIVES, and nothing else.\n\nThis file used to carry a second map, `components`, holding 29 classes that predate the actor library — alert, btn, card, chip, digits, eyebrow, field, ghost, label, lede, logo, mark, meta, panel, step, title, well and the rest. They were kept, deliberately, while call sites still named them: 222 across the website, the checkout, avenID and the app.\n\nThat count is now zero. Every one of those surfaces renders from actors, so the superseded map is deleted rather than deprecated — a clean-slate architecture does not ship its own transition scaffolding. `app-shell` is the one survivor and it moved UP, into layouts, because that is what it always was.",
	"components": {},
